course: dictionary
lesson: 15652
title: An old word: therefor
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Therefor» is a very old word. You will almost only see it in legal papers, like contracts, or in old books. It means «for that» or «for it». In «the goods and the payment therefor», therefor means the payment for them.
explain: Do not use «therefor» in your own writing. Its spelling looks like «therefore», but «therefore» is the common word that means «so» or «for that reason», as in «It rained, therefore we stayed in.»
explain: To check the meaning, swap in «for it» or «for that». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «The price therefor» becomes «the price for it».
fact: «Therefor» means for that or for it.
fact: «Therefor» is archaic: it is old-fashioned and rarely used today.
fact: «Therefor» is mostly found in legal papers, such as contracts and rules.
fact: «Therefore» is the everyday word that means «so» or «for that reason».
fact: A quick check: if you can swap in «for it» and the sentence still works, «therefor» is probably right.
exercise: «The shop sold us a lamp, and we paid the price therefor.» What does therefor mean here? | In a hurry | *For it, meaning the lamp | Before that | Far away
exercise: «The goods and the payment therefor» means the goods and the payment for them. Which words could replace therefor? | In the box | Very fast | By the sea | *For them
exercise: Which word should Sam use in his story? «It was late, ___ we went home.» | therefor | *therefore | for it | therefors
test: «The council charged a fee, and the applicant paid the fee therefor.» What does therefor mean? | *For that fee | Free of charge | A kind of stamp | Before the council met
test: Which word is the best modern choice in your own writing? «The bus was cancelled; ___ we walked.» | therefor | tomorrow | then | *therefore
exam: «The goods were damaged, and the seller refunded the cost therefor.» What does therefor mean? | *For them | Behind the door | Very carefully | In a loud voice
